# Build context is the repo root (docker/docker-compose.yml sets `context: ..`).
# docker/Dockerfile copies exactly: mix.exs, mix.lock, config/, lib/, priv/ and frontend/.
# Everything below is host-side state that must not be uploaded to the daemon — either
# because it is large, because it is a secret, or because a stale copy of it would end up
# inside the image.

# Elixir build state. Rebuilt inside the image; host artifacts are the wrong OTP/glibc
# anyway, and _build + deps dominate the context size.
_build
deps
cover
doc
*.ez
erl_crash.dump

# Locally built SPA. Stage 1 always rebuilds it and COPYs its dist over priv/static/spa,
# but that merge only overwrites same-named files: a host copy would leak everything the
# fresh build has no counterpart for — in particular the `.gz` variants that
# scripts/build-frontend.sh adds and vite does not, which Plug.Static serves in preference
# to the plain file. The image would then ship stale JavaScript.
priv/static/spa

# Runtime data: the SQLite DB and the generated root secrets live in the termix-data
# volume, never in an image layer.
db
priv/tmp
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.env
.env.*

# Frontend: the source is required (stage 1 builds it), its build state is not. Docker only
# honours the .dockerignore at the context root, so the frontend checkout's own is inert.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/db
frontend/*.db*
frontend/release
frontend/coverage

# VCS, editor and agent metadata.
**/.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Not part of the release build.
test
scripts
docs
*.md
